<p>As for Fall 2027, incoming students at the University of Wyoming will no longer be allowed to major in philosophy.<span id="more-57909"></span></p>
<p>The news was shared by philosophy professor <a href="https://bradleyrettler.wixsite.com/home" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bradley Rettler</a> in <a href="https://x.com/rettlerb/status/2080029466257137999" target="_blank" rel="noopener">posts on social media</a>.</p>
<p>He says that students will be able to major in &#8220;philosophy and religion&#8221; but not &#8220;philosophy&#8221; nor &#8220;religious studies&#8221;.</p>
<p>Rettler points out just how unusual this is:</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;"><em>Wyoming will become the first state in the US where you cannot receive a B.A. in Philosophy. The University of Wyoming will be the only R1 institution, the only state flagship university, and one of two land-grant universities that do not offer a B.A. in Philosophy.</em></p>
<p>It is unclear what the justification for this decision is.</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="wp-image-57912 aligncenter" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/wyoming-cuts-philosophy-major-1024x679.png" alt="" width="702" height="466" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/wyoming-cuts-philosophy-major-1024x679.png 1024w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/wyoming-cuts-philosophy-major-300x199.png 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/wyoming-cuts-philosophy-major-768x510.png 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/wyoming-cuts-philosophy-major-1536x1019.png 1536w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/wyoming-cuts-philosophy-major-400x265.png 400w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/wyoming-cuts-philosophy-major.png 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 702px) 100vw, 702px" /></p>
<p>The university administration has led the institution to a situation in which it is facing a <a href="https://wyofile.com/university-of-wyoming-faces-15-million-budget-shortfall/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">$15 million budget shortfall</a>.  Yet philosophy faculty at Wyoming are already part of a joint <a href="https://www.uwyo.edu/philrelig/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Philosophy and Religious Studies department</a>. It is unclear how much additional revenue could be saved, if any, by depriving students of the opportunity to major in philosophy.</p>
<p>It is not known at this time whether the program cut is a prelude to layoffs of philosophy faculty at Wyoming.</p><p>The post <a href="https://dailynous.com/2026/07/23/university-of-wyoming-to-drop-philosophy-major/">University of Wyoming to Drop Philosophy Major</a> first appeared on <a href="https://dailynous.com">Daily Nous</a>.</p>